(window.GROUP_QUIZZES=window.GROUP_QUIZZES||{})["anatomy-exam-3-male-reproductive-quiz-version-7"]={"title":"Male Reproductive System — Anatomy Exam 3 (Set 7)","category":"Anatomy","exam":"Exam 3","sem":"summer-1-2026","questions":[{"q":"The three regions of the male urethra, in order from the bladder outward, are the prostatic, membranous, and:","choices":["Navicular urethra","Ejaculatory urethra","Bulbous urethral segment","Spongy (penile) urethra"],"answer":3,"exp":"The three regions of the male urethra are the prostatic, membranous, and spongy (penile) urethra. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 51"},{"q":"Which region of the male urethra passes through the muscular wall of the pelvic cavity?","choices":["Membranous urethra","Prostatic urethra","Spongy urethra segment","Ejaculatory duct"],"answer":0,"exp":"The membranous urethra passes through the muscular wall of the pelvic cavity. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 51"},{"q":"The three accessory glands of the male reproductive system are the seminal glands, the prostate, and the:","choices":["The paired adrenal glands","The thyroid gland lobes","Bulbo-urethral (Cowper's) glands","The parathyroid glands"],"answer":2,"exp":"The three accessory glands are the seminal glands (vesicles), the prostate, and the bulbo-urethral (Cowper's) glands. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 53"},{"q":"The bulbo-urethral glands are paired structures located at which site?","choices":["Within the epididymis","The apex of the prostate","Within the scrotum","The base of the penis"],"answer":3,"exp":"The bulbo-urethral (Cowper's) glands are paired glands located at the base of the penis. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 57"},{"q":"Contents of the bulbo-urethral glands empty into the spongy urethra at a location immediately distal to the end of which structure?","choices":["The ampulla of the vas","The ejaculatory duct","The membranous urethra","The prostatic urethra"],"answer":2,"exp":"Bulbo-urethral gland contents empty into the spongy urethra immediately distal to the end of the membranous urethra (the body wall). — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 57"},{"q":"According to the lecture, each ejaculation releases approximately how much semen?","choices":["20 to 25 mL","10 to 15 mL","0.5 to 1 mL","2 to 5 mL"],"answer":3,"exp":"Each ejaculation releases approximately 2 to 5 mL of semen. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 59"},{"q":"According to the lecture, a normal sperm count ranges from approximately how many sperm per mL?","choices":["1 to 2 billion","20 to 100 million","1 to 5 million","200 to 500 million"],"answer":1,"exp":"A normal sperm count ranges from approximately 20 to 100 million per mL. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 59"},{"q":"Of the total seminal fluid volume, approximately what percentage comes from the epididymis, per the lecture's breakdown?","choices":["5 percent","15 percent","60 percent","30 percent"],"answer":0,"exp":"About 5 percent of seminal fluid volume comes from the epididymis, per the lecture's breakdown (60% seminal vesicles, 30% prostate, 5% bulbo-urethral glands, 5% epididymis). — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 59"},{"q":"The three regions of the penis are the root, the body (shaft), and the:","choices":["The corona","Penile bulb","Glans penis","The crus base"],"answer":2,"exp":"The three regions of the penis are the root, the body (shaft), and the glans penis. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 60"},{"q":"The root of the penis attaches the base of the penis to which bony structure?","choices":["The base of the sacrum","The rami of the ischia","The pubic symphysis","The tip of the coccyx"],"answer":1,"exp":"The root of the penis attaches the base of the penis to the rami of the ischia. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 60"},{"q":"The glans penis is the expanded distal end of the penis that surrounds which structure?","choices":["The paired corpora cavernosa","The corpus spongiosum only","The external urethral orifice","The crus of the penis base"],"answer":2,"exp":"The glans penis is the expanded distal end of the penis, surrounding the external urethral orifice. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 60"},{"q":"The penis contains two posterior corpora cavernosa and how many anterior corpus spongiosum columns?","choices":["Three","One","Four","Two"],"answer":1,"exp":"The penis contains two posterior corpora cavernosa and one anterior corpus spongiosum. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 61"},{"q":"The deep artery of the penis runs through the center of which erectile structure?","choices":["The corpus spongiosum","The bulb of the penis","The corpora cavernosa","The glans penis"],"answer":2,"exp":"The deep artery of the penis runs through the center of each corpus cavernosum. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 62"},{"q":"Each corpus cavernosum extends posteriorly to form a structure called the crus of the penis, which is bound to which bone?","choices":["The pubic bone body","The ramus of the ischium","The ilium bone wing","The sacral bone base"],"answer":1,"exp":"Each crus of the penis, the posterior extension of a corpus cavernosum, is bound to the ramus of the ischium. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 62"},{"q":"The thickened, proximal end of the corpus spongiosum forms which structure?","choices":["The glans penis","The prepuce","The crus of the penis","The bulb of the penis"],"answer":3,"exp":"The thickened, proximal end of the corpus spongiosum forms the bulb of the penis. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 62"},{"q":"The prepuce (foreskin), which attaches to the neck of the glans, surrounds which part of the penis?","choices":["The body (shaft) only","The root","The bulb","The tip"],"answer":3,"exp":"The prepuce surrounds the tip of the penis, attaching at the neck of the glans. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 63"},{"q":"Preputial glands located in the skin of the neck of the glans and inner foreskin secrete which substance?","choices":["Smegma","Prostatic fluid","Seminalplasmin","Seminal fluid"],"answer":0,"exp":"Preputial glands secrete a waxy substance called smegma. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 63"},{"q":"According to the lecture's organizational overview, the reproductive system is composed of gonads, a reproductive tract, accessory glands, and which additional component?","choices":["The urinary bladder","The adrenal glands","External genitalia","The kidneys"],"answer":2,"exp":"The reproductive system's four components are the gonads, reproductive tract, accessory glands, and external genitalia (perineal structures). — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 4"},{"q":"In the male reproductive tract, which three structures are involved in the functional maturation, nourishment, storage, and transport of sperm?","choices":["Testis, epididymis, ductus deferens","Testis, urethra, seminal gland","Ductus deferens, urethra, prostate","Epididymis, ductus deferens, urethra"],"answer":3,"exp":"The male reproductive tract, responsible for sperm maturation/storage/transport, consists of the epididymis, ductus deferens, and urethra. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 41"},{"q":"In cross-section, the lecture's figure labels a dorsal artery, dorsal vein, and dorsal nerve on the penis, distinct from which other named penile vessel?","choices":["The internal pudendal artery","The deferential artery","The deep artery of the penis","The testicular artery"],"answer":2,"exp":"The dorsal artery/vein/nerve are shown distinct from the deep artery of the penis, which runs centrally through the corpora cavernosa. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 65"},{"q":"According to the lecture's cross-sectional figure, the erectile tissue of the penis is surrounded by which fibrous layer?","choices":["A collagenous sheath","Dartos fascia","Tunica albuginea only","Cremasteric fascia"],"answer":0,"exp":"The lecture's cross-sectional figure labels a collagenous sheath surrounding the erectile tissue of the penis. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 65"},{"q":"Which muscle is shown surrounding the spongy urethra at the bulb of the penis in the lecture's anatomical figure?","choices":["Ischiocavernosus","Bulbospongiosus","Dartos","Cremaster"],"answer":1,"exp":"The bulbospongiosus muscle is shown surrounding the spongy urethra at the bulb of the penis. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 49"},{"q":"The lecture's cross-sectional figure of the male pelvis labels the triangular area at the base of the urinary bladder, adjacent to the prostate, as the:","choices":["Fundus","Neck","Apex","Trigone"],"answer":3,"exp":"The trigone of the urinary bladder is labeled in the lecture's figure, adjacent to the seminal gland and prostate. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 65"},{"q":"The lecture's figure labels the internal urethral orifice at the junction of the urethra with which structure?","choices":["The bulbo-urethral gland","The spongy urethra","The prostate","The urinary bladder"],"answer":3,"exp":"The internal urethral orifice marks the junction between the urinary bladder and the urethra. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 49"},{"q":"The ejaculatory duct is formed by the union of the ampulla of the ductus deferens and which other structure?","choices":["The efferent ductule of the testis","The excretory duct of the seminal gland","The prostatic urethra itself","The rete testis tubular network"],"answer":1,"exp":"The ejaculatory duct forms from the union of the ampulla of the ductus deferens and the excretory duct of the seminal gland. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 50"},{"q":"The seminal glands (seminal vesicles) contribute approximately what percentage of total semen volume?","choices":["80 percent","60 percent","40 percent","20 percent"],"answer":1,"exp":"The seminal glands produce approximately 60 percent of the semen volume. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 55"},{"q":"Seminal fluid from the seminal glands contains a high concentration of fructose, prostaglandins, and which other component?","choices":["Digestive enzymes","Bicarbonate ions alone","Clotting factors","Bile salts"],"answer":2,"exp":"Seminal fluid contains a high concentration of fructose, prostaglandins, and clotting factors. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 55"},{"q":"The prostate contributes approximately what percentage of total semen volume?","choices":["60 percent","About 5 percent","20–30 percent","90 percent"],"answer":2,"exp":"The prostate produces approximately 20–30 percent of the semen volume. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 56"},{"q":"Which accessory gland's secretions are described as weakly acidic, in contrast to the alkaline secretions of the bulbo-urethral glands?","choices":["The seminal glands","The testis","The epididymis","The prostate"],"answer":3,"exp":"The prostate's secretions are described as weakly acidic, distinct from the alkaline mucus of the bulbo-urethral glands. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 56"},{"q":"According to the lecture, the male climacteric — a period of gradually decreasing reproductive capacity — typically occurs between which ages?","choices":["30 and 40","50 and 60","40 and 50","60 and 70"],"answer":1,"exp":"The male climacteric is described as occurring gradually between ages 50 and 60. — HUGHIE Male Reproductive System summer 2026-2.pptx, Slide 68"}]};
